messages:
jamie: Heads up — running into issues when using the SDK from inside our corp VPC behind an HTTP proxy + mutual TLS. Anyone seen streaming hang / socket closed when using a custom base_url?

alex: which SDK version? are you setting the base_url via env or passing it into the client? can you paste a minimal snippet?

jamie: using @alex v0.9.2. quick snippet: ```js
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  base_url: 'https://private.redwood.mycorp',
  apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY,
  proxy: { host: 'proxy.mycorp', port: 3128 },
});
// then client.chat.stream(...).subscribe(...)
```
streaming starts then hangs ~10-15s, then socket closed.

lina: is the corp proxy doing TLS termination + re-mTLS to the backend? we saw that pattern — it breaks connection upgrades for streams. try `agentOptions: { keepAlive: true }` or better: pass an explicit `httpsAgent` (HttpsProxyAgent) to the transport.

jamie: tried `keepAlive: true`, still flaky. also noticed `REDWOOD_API_BASE` env is present in our env — but i passed `base_url` explicitly so i thought that would override.

alex: order of precedence in the SDK: constructor arg > env var > default. however if you don't pass a transport agent and your environment has a proxy, the internal fetch may use the global agent that the proxy intercepts. you need to pass `transportOptions: { agent: httpsAgent }` so the client uses your mTLS-enabled agent.

moya: another gotcha — some corporate proxies add `Expect: 100-continue` or drop `Connection: upgrade` semantics. for streaming we had to ensure headers include `Connection: keep-alive` and strip `Expect`. capturing `curl -v` helped.

jamie: quick curl test: `curl -v --proxy http://proxy:3128 -H 'Authorization: Bearer ...' -N https://private.redwood.mycorp/v1/streams` shows `HTTP/1.1 502` then `Connection reset by peer`. i'll try agent + strip Expect header.

alex: sample using https-proxy-agent + client certs: ```js
const fs = require('fs');
const { HttpsProxyAgent } = require('https-proxy-agent');
const cert = fs.readFileSync('/etc/certs/client.crt');
const key = fs.readFileSync('/etc/certs/client.key');
const agent = new HttpsProxyAgent({ host: 'proxy.mycorp', port: 3128, cert, key, keepAlive: true });
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  base_url: 'https://private.redwood.mycorp',
  transportOptions: { agent },
});
```
that made streaming stable for us in a similar setup. also make sure NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED isn't accidentally set to 0 in prod.

lina: FYI streaming endpoints are non-idempotent so our retry middleware is off for them by default. if the proxy drops mid-stream the SDK won't auto-retry. workaround is short chunked responses or a resumable pattern on server side (cursor). i'm going to open an SDK issue to expose a `retry.onStreamingError` hook.

jamie: :thumbsup: i'll capture tcpdump + curl logs and open an issue with repro. also can someone confirm the base_url precedence? i thought explicit arg was highest.

alex: explicit arg is highest. if you see otherwise please include the repro env — maybe a subtle parsing bug with trailing slash on some codepath. ping me and @lina and i'll instrument it. if it's urgent we can patch priority in next minor release.

deploy-bot: deploy 1764210000 to dev succeeded for `sdk/0.9.3` — includes HttpsProxyAgent example docs (internal).

jamie: thanks all. i'll try the agent + cert path now and report back later today, will attach logs and minimal repro when i open the issue.
